# Target C-II — complete linear-by-linear train rectangle through `t<=1.86875`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only high-`t` structural propagation  
**Scope:** canonical full-core/no-macroscopic-container Type-II branch with `t=(q-k)/D<=1.86875`  
**Dependencies:** coupled paired-remainder O-O path through `1.86875`; audited train-length/terminal-energy inequality; exact stopped-train crossing topology and train ledger  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_high_t_complete_rectangle_t186875.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The `1.86875` path theorem still supplies a linear same-window family of pairwise
noncrossing O-O complete stopped trains.  Although the row density is now small near
the scalar zero of the path architecture, every selected train remains macroscopically
long in the train-crossing graph.  The same interval/right-endpoint argument used at
`1.8687` therefore still produces a genuine complete bipartite train rectangle.

There are train families

\[
A_*,B_*
\]

such that

\[
\boxed{|A_*|>0.0000055D-o(D),}
\]

\[
\boxed{|B_*|>0.3135D-o(D),}
\]

with the exact properties:

1. every train in `A_*` crosses every train in `B_*` in one strict rhombus;
2. `A_*` is pairwise noncrossing and is one consecutive block of the live O-O path;
3. `B_*` is pairwise noncrossing.

Hence the crossing graph contains an actual

\[
\boxed{K_{|A_*|,|B_*|}}
\]

with both shores linear in `D` throughout `t<=1.86875`.

## 1. Crossing degree of every selected row

The adaptive path theorem selects each train with terminal directional energy

\[
e_\tau\le0.5857-\delta.
\]

The audited train-length theorem gives

\[
{r_\tau\over D}
\ge1-\delta-{e_\tau\over2}-o(1)
\ge1-{0.5857\over2}-{\delta\over2}-o(1).
\]

At `t<=1.86875`, the exact path certificate gives `delta<0.107+o(1)`.  Therefore

\[
\boxed{r_\tau>0.6536D-o(D).}
\]

As before, each strict rhombus on `tau` is one crossing with a distinct complete
stopped train, so the crossing neighborhood satisfies

\[
|\Gamma(\tau)|>0.6536D-o(D).
\]

## 2. The path still has linear length

The exact `1.86875` paired-remainder certificate gives total selected low-energy pair
weight above `0.00016D-o(D)`.  One of at most three dominant phase windows therefore
contains more than

\[
\boxed{0.00005D-o(D)}
\]

actual same-window O-O path trains.  Write them in complement-dual order as

\[
\tau_1,\ldots,\tau_m,
\qquad
m>0.00005D-o(D).
\]

For every complete train `sigma`, the set of selected rows crossed by `sigma` is one
consecutive interval, exactly as in the `1.8687` rectangle theorem.

## 3. Nine-block endpoint averaging

The exact stopped-train ledger gives

\[
{T_{tr}\over D}
\le5T-2\pi+o(1).
\]

At `T=1.86875`, the companion certificate proves

\[
\boxed{T_{tr}<3.0606D+o(D).}
\]

Partition the selected path into nine consecutive blocks.  Each block contains more
than

\[
{0.00005\over9}D-o(D)>0.0000055D-o(D)
\]

selected rows.  Assign every nonempty crossing interval to the block containing its
right endpoint.  Some block `J` receives fewer than

\[
{3.0606\over9}D+o(D)
\]

right endpoints.

Let `tau_a` be the first row of `J`.  More than `0.6536D-o(D)` trains cross it.  A train
crossing `tau_a` but failing to cross all of `J` must end inside `J`, hence is charged
to one of those right endpoints.  Therefore the common crossing family obeys

\[
\begin{aligned}
\left|\bigcap_{j\in J}\Gamma(\tau_j)\right|
&>\left(0.6536-{3.0606\over9}\right)D-o(D)\\
&>0.3135D-o(D).
\end{aligned}
\]

Take this intersection as `B_*` and the rows of `J` as `A_*`.

## 4. Internal noncrossing is unchanged

The rows are a subfamily of the pairwise noncrossing O-O path.  If two columns in
`B_*` crossed one another, then together with any row of `A_*` they would form a
triangle in the complete-train crossing graph.  That graph is triangle-free.
Therefore `B_*` is pairwise noncrossing.

The orientation-ambiguity argument from the `1.8687` phase theorem also immediately
gives one consistent oriented column subfamily of density

\[
\boxed{>0.1567D-o(D).}
\]

after deleting only `O(1)` ambiguous columns.  The inverse-`D` phase-collapse
propagation is recorded separately so its larger numerical constant is not hidden in
this rectangle statement.

**Disposition:** proved proof-only complete train rectangle through `t<=1.86875`.
C-II and Level I remain open.
